  "output": {
    "answer": "It's a hardcoded tier ladder, not something the coordinator picks per task: haiku gets reviewed by sonnet, sonnet by opus 4.6, and opus by Fable. The rule is fixed policy, not a judgment call made per lane — review is mandatory before merge, and the reviewer is never a peer of whoever built it. The excerpts don't show the coordinator dynamically selecting a reviewer model on a case-by-case basis; it's the same tier-above rule applied every time.",
